From a532ff728568da49e39295ef7183976be1c10c44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:37:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] Flasher v0.3: write the XD link hook too, in one or
 more spans

The flasher now writes any number of spans (up to four), each with hash
tables for the written state and for each state it may start from: the
dump, or the dump after the v0.2 flash. make_flasher.py builds the target
as the Colosseum program plus the XD hook (Emerald's link code and
linkhook.bin in the unused end of the Colosseum program area) and groups
the changes into spans. Blocks already written are left alone, so a cart
flashed with v0.2 gets only the two blocks that change.

The XD loader index now travels in the loader's own epilogue word (IWRAM)
instead of EWRAM, which Emerald still owns when the hook runs.

The save writer keeps its own six identity ranges and now also skips the
link code area, so it works on carts flashed with v0.2 or v0.3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014JPQshc9oBXnzvR2E67Khm
